    "answer": {
      "short": "A: $30\\%$ profit; B: $25\\%$ profit. Investment A made the higher percentage profit.",
      "worked": "Investment A:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Profit} &= \\$650-\\$500\\\\&=\\$150\\\\\\text{Percentage profit} &= \\frac{150}{500}\\times100\\%\\\\&=30\\%\\end{align*}$$\nInvestment B:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Profit} &= \\$1000-\\$800\\\\&=\\$200\\\\\\text{Percentage profit} &= \\frac{200}{800}\\times100\\%\\\\&=25\\%\\end{align*}$$\nInvestment A made the higher percentage profit because $30\\%>25\\%$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
